# Github Faves — local dev vars (DO NOT COMMIT real values)
# Copy to .dev.vars and fill in. Deploy value via: wrangler secret put GITHUB_TOKEN
#
# This is the only secret the Worker needs. There is no OAuth flow: a classic
# PAT with no scopes beyond public_repo works, and authentication to the app
# itself is handled by Cloudflare Access.

# Required. Reads starredRepositories GraphQL + repositoryTopics + README.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Cloudflare Access service token. Needed for LOCAL DEV ONLY, for two reasons:
#   1. `wrangler dev` proxies the remote `AI` binding to the deployed Worker,
#      which sits behind Access — without credentials the dev server refuses
#      to start.
#   2. Lets scripts call the deployed API non-interactively.
# These are read from the process environment by wrangler, so export them
# before `wrangler dev`:
#
#   $env:CLOUDFLARE_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID     = "<id>.access"
#   $env:CLOUDFLARE_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET = "<secret>"
#   npx wrangler dev
#
# Create at: dash.cloudflare.com -> Zero Trust -> Access -> Service Auth
# -> Service Tokens. The Access app's allow policy must include
# { any_valid_service_token: {} } for the token to be accepted.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional. Only needed for `wrangler d1` / `wrangler deploy` if you have not
# already run `wrangler login`.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
